# kalk-top Agent Harness and MCP

Use when the task touches Cursor/Codex workflow, `.cursor/rules`, skills, MCP, hooks, or verification commands.

## Prefer Skills First

- `cursor-codex-harness` — prompts, read order, Definition of Done.
- `context-budget-audit` — rules/skills/token audits.
- `gitnexus-static-repo-intel` — graph/impact (dev-only).
- Domain skills via `.agents/SKILL_ROUTER.md`.

## MCP and Tooling

- Default MCP: `kalk-top-repo-assistant` (contract surface, runtime preflight, route/auth, architecture inputs).
- `playwright` for allowed-host UI smoke when Browser is insufficient.
- Animation MCPs are **not** in project `mcp.json`; use `npm run mcp:framer-motion` / `mcp:animation` if needed.
- Verify MCP hints with file reads and `npm run test:contract` / targeted harnesses.
- Full map: [KALK_TOP_AGENT_HARNESS.md](../../docs/dev/KALK_TOP_AGENT_HARNESS.md).

## Slash Commands

Use `.cursor/commands/` when they match the task: `verify-contract`, `verify-fixtures`, `verify-rest`, `verify-js`, `verify-pack`, `runtime-preflight`.

## Hooks

- `after-file-edit-lint` — `php -l` / `node --check` on canonical paths; optional harness preflight on governance file edits.
- Do not treat hook output as runtime or Gate proof.

## `.cursor/rules` link hygiene

Links in this folder resolve relative to `.cursor/rules/`. Use `../../docs/dev/...` for repo-root documentation paths.
